Z||000017||maryjane||12-28-2001||11:40 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by FieroLisa:<BR><B>All I can say is apparently her feelings of love weren't as true as she thought. Feelings change, even if the sex and romance was great in the beginning of it. Of course things are good in the beginning, thats why you are attracted to the person. But as time goes on, you see what bothers you and annoys you about the person, and same for them. It's just a matter of finding the right blend of annoyances that you want to spend the rest of your life with.<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><BR>Well put, Lisa.But it goes a little further than that. From the male's perspective, we have to learn to trust-no matter what. It may bring bad things, but they probably would have come anyway. The 'she's mine' thing has to be left behind for what it is: A teenager's attitude. You learn as you age that very few things in a personal relationship are really worth arguing over. Give in on the little things; discuss the larger issues. Compromise-compromise-compromise. It'll all even out in the end. How many relationships have I seen end over arguments over trivial things?!!<BR>||||reg||1
